        "title": "Lionel Live Synthesis Study 06",
        "purpose": "Preserve the first specimen where associative live navigation, audience input, historical synthesis, and coalition mapping appear to control the episode more strongly than a source queue.",
        "view": {
          "intent": "node",
          "payload": "node.web.summary",
          "label": "Lionel Live Synthesis Study 06"
        },
        "payload": "node.web.summary",
        "intent": "node",
        "key": "node.web.summary",
        "viewRole": "summary",
        "viewKind": "display",
        "semanticLevel": "summary",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "renderShape": {
          "kind": "markdown"
        },
        "markdown": "# Lionel Live Synthesis Study 06\n\n## Associative Realignment Monologue\n\nA roughly **1:23:00** live stream about political disintegration, changing alliances, Candace Owens, Tucker Carlson, Trump, Israel, Iran, Laura Loomer, and a newly forming ideological coalition.\n\n**1 alarm hook**  \n**1 sponsor break**  \n**many live-chat branches**  \n**repeated explicit returns to the main storyline**  \n**1 historical coalition model**\n\n`ALARM -> CATCH-UP STORY -> TURNING POINT -> BRANCH -> RETURN -> MAP ACTORS -> MAP NETWORK -> BUILD NEW COALITION -> COMMUNITY CLOSE`\n\nThe main thread bends constantly, but it does not disappear.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786058390624,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
    },
