      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "lionel-live-synthesis-study-06"
        },
        "markdown": "# 🧭 Central Observation\n\nStudy 06 is not best explained as a media queue.\n\nIt is a **live associative synthesis** organized around one persistent macro-question:\n\n**What happened to the old political alignment, and what new alignment is forming?**\n\nLionel repeatedly leaves that thread for chat comments, jokes, food, personalities, legal sidebars, historical examples, and fresh actors, then explicitly returns with phrases such as `back to this`, `going back to the storyline`, and `let me go back to what I was saying`.\n\nMost importantly, Lionel describes the behavior himself: `you notice how I go back and forth` and says he can change subjects in mid-sentence. \n\nThat makes associative navigation an observed grammar feature rather than our interpretation alone.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786058390624,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
    },
