        "markdown": "# 2 · Live Catch-Up Narrative\n## 5:39–14:41\n\nLionel says he has spent the day scanning X because it provides the fastest picture of current political activity, then offers a compressed history beginning with Trump's 2016 appeal, the 2020 election, COVID-era censorship, and the later return of Trump. \n\nLive-chat remarks repeatedly interrupt the narrative, including a long probiotic and sauerkraut detour. Lionel explicitly notices the switching himself before returning to the political story. \n\n**Function:** establish shared historical memory while demonstrating the live branch-and-return rhythm.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786058390624,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
    },
