        "markdown": "# 3 · Locate the Turning Point\n## 14:41–25:40\n\nLionel asks repeatedly when the old Trump and MAGA relationship changed, rejects Butler as the answer, and identifies October 7, 2023 as the turning point in his narrative. He then describes changing public reactions to Israel, Gaza, Zionism, lobbying, Iran, and Trump's foreign-policy posture. \n\nHe openly marks uncertainty when speculating about why Trump allegedly changed course, including discussion of blackmail and Epstein theories. \n\n**Function:** turn a diffuse sense of change into a temporal phase transition: `before -> event -> after`.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786058390624,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
    },
