        },
        "markdown": "# 4 · Failed Messengers and the Candace Third Rail\n## 25:40–36:14\n\nLionel evaluates Tucker Carlson's confrontations with Ted Cruz and Mike Huckabee and criticizes figures such as Alan Dershowitz and Ben Shapiro as ineffective messengers for the position they are defending. \n\nHe then shifts to a strategic rule: `pick the hill you want to die on`, asking why public figures attack Candace rather than ignoring or gently dismissing her. \n\nWhen a viewer accuses him of simply liking Candace, Lionel redirects the challenge toward facts, subject matter, cause, and message. \n\n**Function:** evaluate not only arguments but whether engaging an opponent is strategically self-defeating.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786058390624,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
    },
