        "markdown": "# 7 · Distributed Research Funnel\n## 53:29–58:04\n\nLionel describes unknown viewers analyzing film and images in extraordinary detail, including an example where an apparent flash was later identified as a reflection. \n\nHe then gives the clearest network description in the study set so far: Candace functions as a **funnel** receiving large numbers of tips, filtering garbage from potentially useful material, while people such as Baron Coleman and other researchers contribute parallel analysis. \n\n**Function:** model the information ecosystem itself, not merely summarize findings produced by it.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786058390624,
