        "markdown": "# 9 · Historical Coalition Model\n## 1:05:30–1:15:22\n\nLionel reaches for political history to explain how coalitions are rebuilt. He describes the Republican Party absorbing Southern Democrats, the religious right, constitutionalists, Tea Party members, Second Amendment groups, and libertarians into a larger tent. \n\nHe argues that a new coalition must again gather people who agree on the issues that matter most, then uses musical genres and crossover artists as an analogy for new political iterations forming from older traditions. \n\n**Function:** convert the observed realignment into a historical model and a political prescription.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
