        "identity": {
          "graphId": "lionel-live-synthesis-study-06"
        },
        "markdown": "# 🧵 New Discovery · Thread Stack\n\nStudy 05 required a **Media Queue**.\n\nStudy 06 requires something different:\n\n## Active Thread Stack\n\nA live speaker can temporarily push a branch onto the discussion without replacing the underlying topic.\n\nExample:\n\n`political realignment`\n\n→ push `viewer probiotic joke`\n\n→ expand `sauerkraut and gut flora`\n\n→ pop branch\n\n→ resume `political realignment`\n\nLater the same mechanism handles Barnes updates, Laura Loomer, farm produce, audience questions, and historical sidebars.\n\nUseful state:\n\n- `primaryThread`\n- `activeBranch`\n- `parentThread`\n- `returnPoint`\n- `branchTrigger`\n- `branchSource`: host, chat, media, memory\n- `status`: active, suspended, resumed, abandoned\n\nThis is closer to a call stack than a playlist.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786058390624,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "lionel-study06-chat",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Live Chat as Navigation Input",
      "root": false,
      "position": {
