        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "lionel-live-synthesis-study-06"
        },
        "markdown": "# 💬 Live Chat as Navigation Input\n\nEarlier studies treated chat largely as rapport or production texture.\n\nHere chat repeatedly changes the route of the analysis.\n\nViewer comments trigger:\n\n- factual clarification\n- jokes and vocabulary tangents\n- Barnes updates\n- challenges to Lionel's Candace position\n- new named actors\n- corrections\n- ideological sidebars\n- requests to revisit earlier subjects\n\nLionel frequently consumes the interruption, comments on it, and then executes a visible return to the prior storyline.\n\nThis suggests a reusable relationship:\n\n**Chat Message -> triggers branch -> Topic Thread**\n\nThe audience is therefore partly an **input device for episode navigation**, not merely an audience.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786058390624,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
    },
