        "identity": {
          "graphId": "lionel-live-synthesis-study-06"
        },
        "markdown": "# 🧲 New Discovery · Coalition Mapping\n\nThe episode repeatedly asks not simply `who agrees?` but:\n\n- who entered the field\n- who defected\n- who lost credibility\n- who agrees only on one issue\n- who remains useful despite disagreement elsewhere\n- which old coalition is breaking\n- which new coalition might replace it\n\nLionel explicitly says he is taking `the best of everybody`, including people from different ideological traditions, because agreement on the important issue can outweigh disagreement elsewhere. \n\nHe later uses Republican coalition history to explain how a new political tent could form. \n\nPossible semantic edges:\n\n- `alignsOn`\n- `divergesOn`\n- `joinsCoalition`\n- `leavesCoalition`\n- `amplifies`\n- `losesTrust`\n- `crossesIdeologicalBoundary`\n- `sharesPriorityWith`",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786058390624,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
    },
