        "identity": {
          "graphId": "lionel-live-synthesis-study-06"
        },
        "markdown": "# 🎛️ Production Grammar\n\nObserved production elements include:\n\n- alarm-style cold open\n- sponsor after the hook\n- live X monitoring as source discovery\n- moderator acknowledgment\n- continuous chat incorporation\n- spontaneous factual or lexical lookup behavior\n- household and personal-life references\n- promotion of Mrs. Lionel's work\n- possible later-stream announcement\n- family-style Sunday closing ritual\n- like, subscribe, and notification request\n\nThe closing metaphor is especially notable: the audience is described as sharing a Sunday feast of ideas. \n\nThat is evidence that community maintenance is not merely a generic YouTube outro. It is part of the show's live identity.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
